            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Catherine Reed"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for St Patrick's day a few years ago, with Irish Cider Cake for Dessert. It's a wonderfully hearty dish. As long as quality (85% pork and above) sausages are used, and good cuts of bacon, I don't really think it needs any more seasoning. Just a twist of salt and black pepper."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "stephanie whitmire"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used Canadian Bacon and breakfast sausage as description says is ok. This dish came out awesome. I followed the directions up until you notice it doesn't tell you when to add the potatoes. Well, since it has to simmer for 30+ minutes, I added the potatoes when I added the liquid. And OMG good. It was so good that my 14 year old who doesn't like anything with a lot of liquid in it asked for more after it was all gone. I suggest if you have 4 or more people making a double batch.",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-04T19:37:23.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BonnieLouwho"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I substituted breakfast sausage for the Irish Sausage and when it was almost done, I added a 1/4 cup milk with 4 tbsp of cornstarch to really thicken up the broth. But that is all I did to this recipe. It was FANTASTIC!!! It tastes the same as the Coddle I ordered at an Irish Pub in Bloomington Indiana! My husband loved it too!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-06T11:43:25.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "4.5 stars but I’m rounding up as this was delicious!! I purchased Whiskey Bangers from my local meat market. I subbed celery for carrots because I wasn’t in the mood to peel more than the potatoes. The milk gets kinda curdlerly but the broth flavor is perfect if you’re sick. I’m not but if I was…wow. It would have hit the spot. Overall - we really enjoyed this on St Patrick’s Day but, I would make this again any weeknight. Thanks wsf!!",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-18T00:59:59.184Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
